      "title": "Types of Economic Activities",
      "explanation": "Goods in markets result from various types of economic activities: primary (e.g., farming for vegetables), secondary (e.g., processing fruits into juices), and tertiary (e.g., selling mobile phones or clothes). These activities transform raw materials into goods that reach consumers.",
